{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794425747,"nonce":"KNPhAh4TENF1FLHlARADYb4pyAQ=","message":"Correction 2026-11-12: the analysis above says the first-party library is 'offered by default (ADR-0076 §5)'. That is out of date: the owner decided on 2026-11-10 that first-party libraries get no special case, no inherent trust and no auto-install. So under (b) an org installs lib:thulasi-ram/build like any library, and an admin grants it the build sandbox explicitly (the same way the clone library gets forge credentials only by an explicit grant). The sandbox must not be granted to the first-party library by default; the Policy over origin is something an admin writes. Cost: a new org cannot build images until an admin installs the library and grants the sandbox, where today 'build:' works with no setup. Worth a sentence in the docs and in the error a 'build:' step gets after the migration.","files":null}]}